  "description": "Fire pools: textured flame sprites around the pool origin (Q12 world position). sprites: [u, v, w, h, tpage, clut, ox, oy] cells of the fire sheets; (ox, oy) is the anchor on the particle. animations: steps [hold, sprite] shown for hold / hold_rate seconds, ending with {\"loop\": step} or {\"stop\": true}. A particle ends on the frame it reaches its stop, but a paused pool keeps it there and draws it every frame: the original read the stop's link as a sprite, so a stop names that sprite (\"sprite\"; the last sprites of the list reproduce those bytes, tpage 0 and sizes far outside the sheet, as on the PS1; omit it to draw nothing). A billboard is sized geom * w / 4 / depth times the particle's scale (Q12); one whose top left corner is left of cull[0] - width, right of cull[1], above cull[2] - height or below cull[3] is not drawn. Behaviours: a fireball falls along its throw until the ground, throws \"embers\" embers, waits land_time and burns (scale times burn_scale); a burn plays Flame from a random step (rand16() / start_divisor), may start its sound, throws a tongue when tongue_sprite shows and a spark when rand16() is 0, and after its time fades by \"fade\" per frame (Q12) for fade_time; embers drift with their speed damped (Q12 factor per frame); tongues, sparks and trails rise until their animation ends; flashes (glow, burst) wait their delay, then play once, fading by \"fade\" per frame after \"wait\" frames. cue: how the scene cues of maps/map7_s03/ending_cues.json throw particles (count = area * rate * time; ring area factor \"area\", brightness (brightness_top - spread) / brightness_divisor; above reseed_above the random generator is reseeded with 0). attached: one flame per bone bone_first..bone_last of the character. Times are Q12 seconds unless said otherwise. Every key is checked. A mod replaces the whole file with its own copy at the same path.",
